RESEARCH METHODOLOGY
The author used qualitative methodology (comparison
and content analysis methods) to evaluate the current
state of open banking in Azerbaijan, its development
history, steps to increase its use potential, and the service
potential of electronic money and payment organizations
licensed by the Central Bank of the Republic of
Azerbaijan. In general, a comparative analysis of the
open banking services of the licensed electronic money
and payment institutions was carried out, and along with
this, examples and inconsistencies related to the approach
to open banking were noted based on a systematic
comparison. Also, the security, use, availability of
explicit consent, API support, and potential and currently
available open banking service support of customer data
related to open banking were investigated in detail using
the content analysis method for electronic money and
payment organizations. The comparative and content
analysis methods ensure that the research reflects the
current real situation regarding open banking in
Azerbaijan, the theoretical value of the obtained results,
and the detailed analysis of the data.
Information about open banking was obtained from
the official website of the Central Bank of the Republic
